nswer-998d1fee-cd59-50fc-a838-c8c38df75103" :answer/id #uuid "998d1fee-cd59-50fc-a838-c8c38df75103" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "first shifting theorem" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09a64570-7366-5af6-914c-e07e6d0e7733" :answer/id #uuid "09a64570-7366-5af6-914c-e07e6d0e7733" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "initial system of ODEs" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27d2dd47-075d-5ea9-91b6-1ba9165b5b78" :answer/id #uuid "27d2dd47-075d-5ea9-91b6-1ba9165b5b78" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "line $\\text{L4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c229293-3ae6-55c9-904e-4831007a77da" :answer/id #uuid "5c229293-3ae6-55c9-904e-4831007a77da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "solution of the system of ODEs" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-61cd9d7f-883b-537f-9ebe-27f46e66ca64" :answer-field/id #uuid "61cd9d7f-883b-537f-9ebe-27f46e66ca64" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ca3d2e76-22e3-519f-9402-f852a4dd6ecd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5e8d746b-dfe9-5dcc-be99-d1e679811b59" "answer-3815ccb0-0a02-5fd6-a641-0b543d3401e6" "answer-c559ce39-ac3e-51a2-87df-019730cfd49f" "answer-ca3d2e76-22e3-519f-9402-f852a4dd6ecd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e8d746b-dfe9-5dcc-be99-d1e679811b59" :answer/id #uuid "5e8d746b-dfe9-5dcc-be99-d1e679811b59" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "adding $Φ$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3815ccb0-0a02-5fd6-a641-0b543d3401e6" :answer/id #uuid "3815ccb0-0a02-5fd6-a641-0b543d3401e6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "differentiating" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c559ce39-ac3e-51a2-87df-019730cfd49f" :answer/id #uuid "c559ce39-ac3e-51a2-87df-019730cfd49f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "integrating" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca3d2e76-22e3-519f-9402-f852a4dd6ecd" :answer/id #uuid "ca3d2e76-22e3-519f-9402-f852a4dd6ecd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a38c17d6-682c-5e64-836d-d5ceddc931f1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a38c17d6-682c-5e64-836d-d5ceddc931f1" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-3bd223f4-079f-5113-98ce-7fccfb02f7de" :answer-field/choices ["answer-87aef158-5bbc-550e-92aa-2b0e8fec0d61" "answer-b1855158-6fc1-5207-a4ea-97cf1edf1b7e" "answer-3bd223f4-079f-5113-98ce-7fccfb02f7de" "answer-16ae9b7b-e430-5eb6-90d6-0e5eeb4fe026"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87aef158-5bbc-550e-92aa-2b0e8fec0d61" :answer/id #uuid "87aef158-5bbc-550e-92aa-2b0e8fec0d61" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "adding $Φ$ to" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1855158-6fc1-5207-a4ea-97cf1edf1b7e" :answer/id #uuid "b1855158-6fc1-5207-a4ea-97cf1edf1b7e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "differentiating" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3bd223f4-079f-5113-98ce-7fccfb02f7de" :answer/id #uuid "3bd223f4-079f-5113-98ce-7fccfb02f7de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "integrating" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16ae9b7b-e430-5eb6-90d6-0e5eeb4fe026" :answer/id #uuid "16ae9b7b-e430-5eb6-90d6-0e5eeb4fe026" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-dc370c50-c95d-53af-9285-c137ac273145" :question/id #uuid "dc370c50-c95d-53af-9285-c137ac273145" :question/math-academy-id "q-336704" :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that {{field-1}} matrix.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines {{field-2}} by substitution.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L7}$ into {{field-3}} ." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L4}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are solutions to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ i.e., by substituting any column $c(t)$ of $Φ$ into the homogeneous system, we get\n\n$$\n{c}^{′}(t)=Ac(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}^{′}(t)$ is the corresponding column of derivatives in $Φ.$ As a result, this means that ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that $Φ\\text{ is a fundamental}$ matrix.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$, $\\text{L4},$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Let's substitute ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$ from $\\text{L4}$ into $\\text{L3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)+\\cancel{AΦu(t)}=\\cancel{AΦu(t)}+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L3}\\text{ and }\\text{L4}$ by substitution.\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L7},$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Substituting\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φu(t) \\\\  & =Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L7}$ into  $\\text{L1}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-345ab8ae-cd66-52b2-9a96-cf0b08ce6895" "answer-field-b0979245-762e-5229-aacd-89b1d72de194" "answer-field-686d35a7-2873-597a-8c04-798dd6392868"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-345ab8ae-cd66-52b2-9a96-cf0b08ce6895" :answer-field/id #uuid "345ab8ae-cd66-52b2-9a96-cf0b08ce6895" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-6cf97b47-a716-5db4-a736-9116713e53e9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-db14b3e6-8255-5b15-af0a-c43b9ec9f0b2" "answer-b732aa44-b145-5c84-9ef0-81ea7fa0094b" "answer-6cf97b47-a716-5db4-a736-9116713e53e9" "answer-f1a583d8-d211-5fa0-9f95-1776becf6650"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db14b3e6-8255-5b15-af0a-c43b9ec9f0b2" :answer/id #uuid "db14b3e6-8255-5b15-af0a-c43b9ec9f0b2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ is an invertible" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b732aa44-b145-5c84-9ef0-81ea7fa0094b" :answer/id #uuid "b732aa44-b145-5c84-9ef0-81ea7fa0094b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ is the identity" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cf97b47-a716-5db4-a736-9116713e53e9" :answer/id #uuid "6cf97b47-a716-5db4-a736-9116713e53e9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Φ$ is a fundamental" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1a583d8-d211-5fa0-9f95-1776becf6650" :answer/id #uuid "f1a583d8-d211-5fa0-9f95-1776becf6650" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Φ$ is a square" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b0979245-762e-5229-aacd-89b1d72de194" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0979245-762e-5229-aacd-89b1d72de194" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-2cb798f6-eb02-5eb0-b90e-3818bf565735" :answer-field/choices ["answer-43cbc5c9-67b9-5e07-8eb7-2a5e0e21e482" "answer-a38f4d63-059b-5216-94a8-f8f05c6278e7" "answer-9e9893e8-8c90-5213-9bbf-617a8a90550e" "answer-2cb798f6-eb02-5eb0-b90e-3818bf565735"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43cbc5c9-67b9-5e07-8eb7-2a5e0e21e482" :answer/id #uuid "43cbc5c9-67b9-5e07-8eb7-2a5e0e21e482" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a38f4d63-059b-5216-94a8-f8f05c6278e7" :answer/id #uuid "a38f4d63-059b-5216-94a8-f8f05c6278e7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e9893e8-8c90-5213-9bbf-617a8a90550e" :answer/id #uuid "9e9893e8-8c90-5213-9bbf-617a8a90550e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2cb798f6-eb02-5eb0-b90e-3818bf565735" :answer/id #uuid "2cb798f6-eb02-5eb0-b90e-3818bf565735" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-686d35a7-2873-597a-8c04-798dd6392868" :answer-field/id #uuid "686d35a7-2873-597a-8c04-798dd6392868" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-dd301c04-28fc-586b-bd66-53538190b1c8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dd301c04-28fc-586b-bd66-53538190b1c8" "answer-e9cb65ee-c4ba-5892-87e8-7031e44aace7" "answer-872cda15-912a-58ab-bcc0-20f624fd722f" "answer-3e47be19-7850-5185-a8be-4f097e3d06a1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd301c04-28fc-586b-bd66-53538190b1c8" :answer/id #uuid "dd301c04-28fc-586b-bd66-53538190b1c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9cb65ee-c4ba-5892-87e8-7031e44aace7" :answer/id #uuid "e9cb65ee-c4ba-5892-87e8-7031e44aace7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-872cda15-912a-58ab-bcc0-20f624fd722f" :answer/id #uuid "872cda15-912a-58ab-bcc0-20f624fd722f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e47be19-7850-5185-a8be-4f097e3d06a1" :answer/id #uuid "3e47be19-7850-5185-a8be-4f097e3d06a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167185 :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]x(t)+\\overset{f(t)}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]}},\\,Φ=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & -3{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & 2{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)$ and the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t)$ of the system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-10{e}^{-2t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{p}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186365601 :answer-field/correct "answer-2014d6d7-4139-5c85-9128-fa0bef9f20e7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2014d6d7-4139-5c85-9128-fa0bef9f20e7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2014d6d7-4139-5c85-9128-fa0bef9f20e7" :answer/id #uuid "2014d6d7-4139-5c85-9128-fa0bef9f20e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4e^{-4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186365803 :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t)+\\overset{f(t)}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]}},\\,Φ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & {e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{3t} & -{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)$ and the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t)$ of the system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{p}(t)={e}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"60px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2{e}^{3t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"60px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{-19}{6}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186365806 :answer-field/correct "answer-fa304d8c-18bb-5d36-ae8a-525a035e8d59" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fa304d8c-18bb-5d36-ae8a-525a035e8d59"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa304d8c-18bb-5d36-ae8a-525a035e8d59" :answer/id #uuid "fa304d8c-18bb-5d36-ae8a-525a035e8d59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5e^{-2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b7f6c605-b7b1-59c8-8433-ca15cc2ba91a" :question/id #uuid "b7f6c605-b7b1-59c8-8433-ca15cc2ba91a" :question/math-academy-id "q-337282" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}]x(t)+\\overset{f(t)}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]}},\\,Φ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-4t} & -{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)$ and the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t)$ of the system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{p}(t)={e}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"60px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"60px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{9}{5}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "We'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-4t} & -{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0\\cdot (-{e}^{2t})-3{e}^{2t}\\cdot {e}^{-4t}}[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{2t} & -3{e}^{2t} \\\\ -{e}^{-4t} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{2t} & -3{e}^{2t} \\\\ -{e}^{-4t} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{4t} & {e}^{4t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-2t} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{4t} & {e}^{4t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-2t} & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{3}{e}^{5t} \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{3}{e}^{5t} \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{7}{3}{e}^{5t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int \\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{15}{e}^{5t} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-4t} & -{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{15}{e}^{5t} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4{e}^{t} \\\\ \\frac{9}{5}{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ \\frac{9}{5}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-898f9d60-0210-5c29-be2c-83afc576e947" "answer-field-bc5b84e5-e81f-590d-82f4-59edebfa2113"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-898f9d60-0210-5c29-be2c-83afc576e947" :answer-field/id #uuid "898f9d60-0210-5c29-be2c-83afc576e947" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f2aca50a-3aaf-509c-a35b-f9a9fcddc26e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f2aca50a-3aaf-509c-a35b-f9a9fcddc26e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2aca50a-3aaf-509c-a35b-f9a9fcddc26e" :answer/id #uuid "f2aca50a-3aaf-509c-a35b-f9a9fcddc26e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}e^{5t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bc5b84e5-e81f-590d-82f4-59edebfa2113" :answer-field/id #uuid "bc5b84e5-e81f-590d-82f4-59edebfa2113" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-fec73258-a6f9-59da-abbe-d2238c0a8b2f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fec73258-a6f9-59da-abbe-d2238c0a8b2f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fec73258-a6f9-59da-abbe-d2238c0a8b2f" :answer/id #uuid "fec73258-a6f9-59da-abbe-d2238c0a8b2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b0ea864c-5060-5aaa-9a4d-f96c65c21a98" :question/id #uuid "b0ea864c-5060-5aaa-9a4d-f96c65c21a98" :question/math-academy-id "q-337277" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t)+\\overset{f(t)}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} \\\\ 5{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]}},\\,Φ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & {e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{2t} & -{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)$ and the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t)$ of the system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{p}(t)={e}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2{e}^{2t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "We'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & {e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{2t} & -{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} \\\\ 5{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0\\cdot (-{e}^{-t})-{e}^{-t}\\cdot {e}^{2t}}[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-t} & -{e}^{-t} \\\\ -{e}^{2t} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-t} & -{e}^{-t} \\\\ -{e}^{2t} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{t} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{t} & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} \\\\ 5{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7{e}^{-t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}7{e}^{-t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int 7{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int 2{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & {e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{2t} & -{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-7{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ -8{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bc64baf6-24fe-50cf-9562-d51c8458064c" "answer-field-d97aac68-90ca-5220-87c6-8339db558421"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bc64baf6-24fe-50cf-9562-d51c8458064c" :answer-field/id #uuid "bc64baf6-24fe-50cf-9562-d51c8458064c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f35ae682-6b7b-5152-aa93-33c0ea7e72cb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f35ae682-6b7b-5152-aa93-33c0ea7e72cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f35ae682-6b7b-5152-aa93-33c0ea7e72cb" :answer/id #uuid "f35ae682-6b7b-5152-aa93-33c0ea7e72cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7e^{-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d97aac68-90ca-5220-87c6-8339db558421" :answer-field/id #uuid "d97aac68-90ca-5220-87c6-8339db558421" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-906cdba8-6fbc-5988-adcc-f889973de75e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-906cdba8-6fbc-5988-adcc-f889973de75e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-906cdba8-6fbc-5988-adcc-f889973de75e" :answer/id #uuid "906cdba8-6fbc-5988-adcc-f889973de75e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311829 :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t)+\\overset{f(t)}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]}},\\,Φ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5{e}^{-3t} \\\\ {e}^{2t} & -4{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)$ and the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t)$ of the system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{p}(t)={e}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"60px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{3}{5}{e}^{4t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"60px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311313 :answer-field/correct "answer-69172624-3326-54b0-b3c7-c380d2de2937" :answer-field/choices ["answer-69172624-3326-54b0-b3c7-c380d2de2937"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69172624-3326-54b0-b3c7-c380d2de2937" :answer/id #uuid "69172624-3326-54b0-b3c7-c380d2de2937" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{22}{5}e^{-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311830 :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations. Using the method of variation of parameters, the general solution of the equation can be written in the form\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+\\,\\,\\frac{1}{9}$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$23-15t$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311833 :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations. Using the method of variation of parameters, the general solution of the equation can be written in the form\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+\\,\\,\\frac{1}{9}$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$39t+23$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167263 :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}6t \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations. Using the method of variation of parameters, the general solution of the equation can be written in the form\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+\\,\\,\\frac{1}{4}$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$36t-42$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nNotice that we are given that\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\nWe'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{-t} \\\\ 3{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}6t \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2{e}^{-2t}\\cdot {e}^{-t}-{e}^{-t}\\cdot 3{e}^{-2t}}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & -{e}^{-t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-2t} & 2{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & -{e}^{-t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-2t} & 2{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & -{e}^{2t} \\\\ -3{e}^{t} & 2{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =-[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & -{e}^{2t} \\\\ -3{e}^{t} & 2{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6t \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 12t{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}-3t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 12t{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int -3t{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int 12t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating the components by parts, we get the following:\n\n- For the first component, let $u=-3t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=-3\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -3t{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(-3t)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}-\\int \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}\\cdot (-3\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}t{e}^{2t}+\\frac{3}{2}\\int {e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}t{e}^{2t}+\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{2t} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{2t}(1-2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, let $u=12t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=12\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v={e}^{t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 12t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t & =12t\\cdot {e}^{t}-\\int 12\\cdot {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =12t{e}^{t}-12{e}^{t} \\\\  & =12{e}^{t}(t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{-t} \\\\ 3{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{2t}(1-2t) \\\\ 12{e}^{t}(t-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}6(1-2t)+48(t-1) \\\\ 9(1-2t)+48(t-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}36t-42 \\\\ 30t-39\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164761 :answer-field/correct "answer-5f0a9736-6f06-5aca-901d-8b514f93cdc9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5f0a9736-6f06-5aca-901d-8b514f93cdc9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f0a9736-6f06-5aca-901d-8b514f93cdc9" :answer/id #uuid "5f0a9736-6f06-5aca-901d-8b514f93cdc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30t-39" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311834 :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations. Using the method of variation of parameters, the general solution of the equation can be written in the form\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+\\,\\,\\frac{1}{9}$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$30t+20$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-858d57fe-416e-56c5-af8b-4ea6e4298062" :question/id #uuid "858d57fe-416e-56c5-af8b-4ea6e4298062" :question/math-academy-id "q-337289" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}5t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations. Using the method of variation of parameters, the general solution of the equation can be written in the form\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+\\,\\,\\frac{1}{9}$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-3t-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nNotice that we are given that\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}.\n$$\n\nWe'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & {e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{-t}\\cdot {e}^{3t}-{e}^{3t}\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & -{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & -{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & -{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & -{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4t{e}^{t} \\\\ t{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}4t{e}^{t} \\\\ t{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int 4t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int t{e}^{-3t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating the components by parts, we get the following:\n\n- For the first component, let $u=4t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=4\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v={e}^{t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(4t)\\cdot {e}^{t}-\\int {e}^{t}\\cdot (4\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =4t{e}^{t}-4{e}^{t} \\\\  & =4{e}^{t}(t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, let $u=t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{-3t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v=-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int t{e}^{-3t}\\,\\text{d}t & =t\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3t})-\\int (-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{t}{3}{e}^{-3t}+\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{-3t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{t}{3}{e}^{-3t}-\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{-3t} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{-3t}(3t+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & {e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{t}(t-1) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{-3t}(3t+1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}36(t-1)-(3t+1) \\\\ -(3t+1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}33t-37 \\\\ -3t-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9324a6eb-07ab-5ed4-84d0-646338f3a965"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9324a6eb-07ab-5ed4-84d0-646338f3a965" :answer-field/id #uuid "9324a6eb-07ab-5ed4-84d0-646338f3a965" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a8039f17-10a2-5a2d-8787-b1e6d3df2d80" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a8039f17-10a2-5a2d-8787-b1e6d3df2d80"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8039f17-10a2-5a2d-8787-b1e6d3df2d80" :answer/id #uuid "a8039f17-10a2-5a2d-8787-b1e6d3df2d80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "33t-37" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167991 :tutorial/content "Consider the system of ordinary differential equations\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}'(t) =\nA\n\\mathbf{x}(t) +\n\\mathbf{f}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a constant square matrix and $\\mathbf{f}(t)$ is a forcing vector.\n\nIn this lesson, we'll derive the formula for the particular solution of the above system using the method of variation of parameters.\n\nRecall that the general solution of the corresponding homogeneous system is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}_c(t)  = \\Phi \\, \\mathbf{c}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{c}$ is a vector of constants, and $\\Phi$ is the fundamental matrix.\n\nAs usual, for the method of variation of parameters, we'll look for a particular solution of our inhomogeneous system by varying the constant parameters, i.e., in the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}_p(t)  = \\Phi \\, \\mathbf{u}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{u}(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined.\n\nDifferentiating $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =(Φ\\,u(t))^{′} \\\\  & =Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ is a solution, substituting it back into the initial system gives a true equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =Ax(t)+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t) & =AΦu(t)+f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, since $\\Phi$ is a fundamental matrix, $\\Phi' = A \\Phi.$ Substituting this into the equation simplifies it to the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ{u}^{′}(t)+AΦu(t) & =AΦu(t)+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t) & =f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since $\\Phi$ is invertible, we can pre-multiply both sides by $\\Phi^{-1}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\cdot Φ{u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate both sides of the final equations (ignoring the constant term):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}_p(t) = \\Phi \\displaystyle\\int \\Phi^{-1}\\mathbf{f}(t) \\, \\text{d}t.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166985 :activity/expected-seconds 1500.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186061086 :answer-field/choices 17592186061088] [:db/retract 17592186061086 :answer-field/choices 17592186061089] [:db/retract 17592186061086 :answer-field/choices 17592186061090] [:db/retract 17592186061086 :answer-field/choices 17592186061091] [:db/retract 17592186061086 :answer-field/choices 17592186061087] {:db/id 17592186064247 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f8a011fe-bff7-586f-86e9-fabb797df0e3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064002 :question/problem "Factor the quadratic expression $10a^2 + 11a + 3.$" :question/worked-solution "We must factor the quadratic expression\n\n$$\n10a^2 + 11a + 3.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find two numbers that \n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant ($10 \\times 3 = 30$), and\n\n- add to the linear coefficient ($11$).\n\nSince all coefficients are positive, we only need to consider the positive factor pairs of $30.$\n\nThe positive factor pairs of $30$ are\n\n$$\n(1,30), \\quad (2,15), \\quad (3,10), \\quad (5,6).\n$$\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(5,6)$ add to $11{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5+6 & =11\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we write the linear term as $5a + 6a,$ and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10{a}^{2}+11a+3 & = \\\\ 10{a}^{2}+5a+6a+3 & = \\\\ (10{a}^{2}+5a)+(6a+3) & = \\\\ 5a(2a+1)+3(2a+1) & = \\\\ (5a+3)(2a+1) & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064248 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d54b0636-ad05-55a6-91c9-9613b500f9d1" "question-433698fd-3b83-5c8a-9280-a485202f8699"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064004 :question/problem "Factor the quadratic expression $2c^2 + 15c - 8.$" :question/worked-solution "We must factor the quadratic expression\n\n$$\n2c^2 + 15c - 8.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find two numbers that \n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant ($2 \\times -8 = -16$), and\n\n- add to the linear coefficient ($15$).\n\nFirst, we find the factor pairs of $-16{:}$\n\n$$\n(1,-16),\\quad (-1,16), \\quad (2,-8), \\quad (-2,8), \\quad (4,-4)\n$$\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(-1,16)$ add to $15{:}$ \n\n$$\n(-1) + 16 = 15 \\quad {\\color{green}\\checkmark}\n$$\n\nThen, rewrite the linear term as $- c+16c,$ and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{c}^{2}+15c-8 & = \\\\ 2{c}^{2}-c+16c-8 & = \\\\ (2{c}^{2}-c)+(16c-8) & = \\\\ c(2c-1)+8(2c-1) & = \\\\ (2c-1)(c+8) & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064249 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3b50cd1f-80a5-51f1-b3eb-2663a6e28812"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064003 :question/problem "Factor the expression $3x^2 - 16x + 16.$" :question/worked-solution "We must factor the quadratic expression\n\n$$\n3x^2 - 16x + 16.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find two numbers that \n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant ($3 \\times 16 = 48$), and\n\n- add to the linear coefficient ($-16$).\n\nSince the linear coefficient is negative and the product of the quadratic coefficient and constant is positive, we only need to consider the negative factor pairs of $48.$\n\nThe negative factor pairs of $48$ are\n\n$$\n(-1,-48), \\quad (-2,-24), \\quad (-3,-16), \\quad (-4,-12), \\quad (-6,-8).\n$$\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(-4,-12)$ add to $-16{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-4)+(-12) & =-16\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we write the linear term as $-4x - 12x,$ and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-16x+16 & = \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-4x-12x+16 & = \\\\ (3{x}^{2}-4x)-(12x-16) & = \\\\ x(3x-4)-4(3x-4) & = \\\\ (x-4)(3x-4) & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064476 :question/problem "$6{w}^{2}+19w+10=$" :question/worked-solution "We must factor the quadratic expression\n\n$$\n6{w}^{2}+19w+10.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find two numbers that \n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant ($6\\times 10=60$), and\n\n- add to the linear coefficient ($19$).\n\nSince all coefficients are positive, we only need to consider the positive factor pairs of $60.$\n\nThe positive factor pairs of $60$ are\n\n$$\n(1,60),\\,(2,30),\\,(3,10),\\,(4,15),\\,(5,12),\\,(6,10).\n$$\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(4,15)$ add to $19:$ \n\n$$\n4+15=19\\,✓\n$$\n\nThen, we write the linear term as $4w+15w,$ and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{w}^{2}+19w+10 & = \\\\ 6{w}^{2}+4w+15w+10 & = \\\\ (6{w}^{2}+4w)+(15w+10) & = \\\\ 2w(3w+2)+5(3w+2) & = \\\\ (3w+2)(2w+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186061086 :answer-field/correct "answer-dfbd19af-9737-539e-b11a-593a8a2fa762" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a8505418-0dab-57f8-904d-143d5e551a21" "answer-dfbd19af-9737-539e-b11a-593a8a2fa762" "answer-139e2599-d442-5bcf-9fed-9beb770bdac1" "answer-0f956e5b-1886-5c73-b8bc-cf07f5514c55" "answer-47b0fd5d-4c37-52f2-9295-22a8f59254c4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8505418-0dab-57f8-904d-143d5e551a21" :answer/id #uuid "a8505418-0dab-57f8-904d-143d5e551a21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3w+10)(2w+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfbd19af-9737-539e-b11a-593a8a2fa762" :answer/id #uuid "dfbd19af-9737-539e-b11a-593a8a2fa762" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3w+2)(2w+5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-139e2599-d442-5bcf-9fed-9beb770bdac1" :answer/id #uuid "139e2599-d442-5bcf-9fed-9beb770bdac1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3w+5)(2w+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f956e5b-1886-5c73-b8bc-cf07f5514c55" :answer/id #uuid "0f956e5b-1886-5c73-b8bc-cf07f5514c55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(6w+1)(w+10)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47b0fd5d-4c37-52f2-9295-22a8f59254c4" :answer/id #uuid "47b0fd5d-4c37-52f2-9295-22a8f59254c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(3w+1)(w+5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f8a011fe-bff7-586f-86e9-fabb797df0e3" :question/id #uuid "f8a011fe-bff7-586f-86e9-fabb797df0e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-111838" :question/problem "$10{m}^{2}+13m+4=$" :question/worked-solution "We must factor the quadratic expression\n\n$$\n10{m}^{2}+13m+4.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find two numbers that \n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant ($10\\times 4=40$), and\n\n- add to the linear coefficient ($13$).\n\nSince all coefficients are positive, we only need to consider the positive factor pairs of $40.$\n\nThe positive factor pairs of $40$ are\n\n$$\n(1,40),\\,(2,20),\\,(4,10),\\,(5,8).\n$$\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(5,8)$ add to $13:$ \n\n$$\n5+8=13\\,✓\n$$\n\nThen, we write the linear term as $5m+8m,$ and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10{m}^{2}+13m+4 & = \\\\ 10{m}^{2}+5m+8m+4 & = \\\\ (10{m}^{2}+5m)+(8m+4) & = \\\\ 5m(2m+1)+4(2m+1) & = \\\\ (5m+4)(2m+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-baaf1380-7960-5d0a-861f-dfdf49029a8a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-baaf1380-7960-5d0a-861f-dfdf49029a8a" :answer-field/id #uuid "baaf1380-7960-5d0a-861f-dfdf49029a8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3f3f1441-07e1-5f0d-b9d6-5cbf147a0251" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c51f24dc-3a4d-52e8-b926-ba0e14c2c0e2" "answer-0617ff8b-9a53-5a85-9776-ca14a6b5a1e2" "answer-3f3f1441-07e1-5f0d-b9d6-5cbf147a0251" "answer-d5ca640d-8f6e-53a9-b58a-e4f953665ac9" "answer-a9dba60b-09d4-5767-814a-20971c8a355a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c51f24dc-3a4d-52e8-b926-ba0e14c2c0e2" :answer/id #uuid "c51f24dc-3a4d-52e8-b926-ba0e14c2c0e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(10m+1)(m+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0617ff8b-9a53-5a85-9776-ca14a6b5a1e2" :answer/id #uuid "0617ff8b-9a53-5a85-9776-ca14a6b5a1e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5m+1)(m+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f3f1441-07e1-5f0d-b9d6-5cbf147a0251" :answer/id #uuid "3f3f1441-07e1-5f0d-b9d6-5cbf147a0251" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5m+4)(2m+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5ca640d-8f6e-53a9-b58a-e4f953665ac9" :answer/id #uuid "d5ca640d-8f6e-53a9-b58a-e4f953665ac9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(5m+1)(m+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9dba60b-09d4-5767-814a-20971c8a355a" :answer/id #uuid "a9dba60b-09d4-5767-814a-20971c8a355a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(5m+2)(m+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d54b0636-ad05-55a6-91c9-9613b500f9d1" :question/id #uuid "d54b0636-ad05-55a6-91c9-9613b500f9d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-224935" :question/problem "Factor the following quadratic expression.\n\n$5{b}^{2}-34b-7=(b\\,-$\n{{field-1}}$)($\n{{field-2}}$b\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "We must factor the quadratic expression\n\n$$\n5{b}^{2}-34b-7.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find two numbers that \n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant ($5\\times -7=-35$), and\n\n- add to the linear coefficient ($-34$).\n\nFirst, we find the factor pairs of $-35:$\n\n$$\n(1,-35),\\,(-1,35),\\,(5,-7),\\,(-5,7)\n$$\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(1,-35)$ add to $-34:$ \n\n$$\n1+(-35)=-34\\,✓\n$$\n\nThen, rewrite the linear term as $b-35b,$ and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{b}^{2}-34b-7 & = \\\\ 5{b}^{2}+b-35b-7 & = \\\\ (5{b}^{2}+b)-(35b+7) & = \\\\ b(5b+1)-7(5b+1) & = \\\\ (b-7)(5b+1) & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-15fd5e31-0a26-515f-9010-378807b928a9" "answer-field-6d81b9e9-cd19-5eec-9e3c-c8f9eb596d52" "answer-field-8b2c159e-029b-5def-beed-5f2e79c867bd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-15fd5e31-0a26-515f-9010-378807b928a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "15fd5e31-0a26-515f-9010-378807b928a9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-906a0b55-204a-56a6-a903-6f001989e184" :answer-field/choices ["answer-906a0b55-204a-56a6-a903-6f001989e184"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-906a0b55-204a-56a6-a903-6f001989e184" :answer/id #uuid "906a0b55-204a-56a6-a903-6f001989e184" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6d81b9e9-cd19-5eec-9e3c-c8f9eb596d52" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d81b9e9-cd19-5eec-9e3c-c8f9eb596d52" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-236446a4-7281-5c03-903f-c5084de03781" :answer-field/choices ["answer-236446a4-7281-5c03-903f-c5084de03781"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-236446a4-7281-5c03-903f-c5084de03781" :answer/id #uuid "236446a4-7281-5c03-903f-c5084de03781" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8b2c159e-029b-5def-beed-5f2e79c867bd" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b2c159e-029b-5def-beed-5f2e79c867bd" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-18be1f63-741d-5018-91f5-2810be8a6b0e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-18be1f63-741d-5018-91f5-2810be8a6b0e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18be1f63-741d-5018-91f5-2810be8a6b0e" :answer/id #uuid "18be1f63-741d-5018-91f5-2810be8a6b0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-433698fd-3b83-5c8a-9280-a485202f8699" :question/id #uuid "433698fd-3b83-5c8a-9280-a485202f8699" :question/math-academy-id "q-52254" :question/problem "Factor $5{h}^{2}-12h-9.$" :question/worked-solution "We must factor the quadratic expression\n\n$$\n5{h}^{2}-12h-9.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find two numbers that \n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant ($5\\times -9=-45$), and\n\n- add to the linear coefficient ($-12$).\n\nThe factor pairs of $-45$ are\n\n$$\n(1,-45),\\,\\,(-1,45),\\,\\,(3,-15),\\,\\,(-3,15),\\,\\,(5,-9),\\,\\,(-5,9).\n$$\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(3,-15)$ add to $-12:$ \n\n$$\n3-15=-12\\,✓\n$$\n\nThen, rewrite the linear term as $3h-15h,$ and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{h}^{2}-12h-9 & = \\\\ 5{h}^{2}+3h-15h-9 & = \\\\ 5{h}^{2}-15h+3h-9 & = \\\\ (5{h}^{2}-15h)+(3h-9) & = \\\\ 5h(h-3)+3(h-3) & = \\\\ (5h+3)(h-3) & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-37c5d472-7e62-5f47-b3dc-73ce05638ddc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-37c5d472-7e62-5f47-b3dc-73ce05638ddc" :answer-field/id #uuid "37c5d472-7e62-5f47-b3dc-73ce05638ddc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-83ff1739-d53c-5c8a-bb8e-be1d8a7c3c55" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f1e12de1-9652-519c-a92a-edcd7c96464d" "answer-f61fabd3-a06c-5ead-8f35-37c1f39d63e2" "answer-e66b9ced-ce85-5b70-a931-a9180edc99f1" "answer-83ff1739-d53c-5c8a-bb8e-be1d8a7c3c55" "answer-7d31edaf-e68f-5896-886f-ba0c8884747c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1e12de1-9652-519c-a92a-edcd7c96464d" :answer/id #uuid "f1e12de1-9652-519c-a92a-edcd7c96464d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5h+1)(h-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f61fabd3-a06c-5ead-8f35-37c1f39d63e2" :answer/id #uuid "f61fabd3-a06c-5ead-8f35-37c1f39d63e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5h+1)(h-9)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e66b9ced-ce85-5b70-a931-a9180edc99f1" :answer/id #uuid "e66b9ced-ce85-5b70-a931-a9180edc99f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5h+3)(h-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83ff1739-d53c-5c8a-bb8e-be1d8a7c3c55" :answer/id #uuid "83ff1739-d53c-5c8a-bb8e-be1d8a7c3c55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5h+3)(h-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d31edaf-e68f-5896-886f-ba0c8884747c" :answer/id #uuid "7d31edaf-e68f-5896-886f-ba0c8884747c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5h-3)(h+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064616 :question/problem "Factor the following quadratic expression.\n\n$4{x}^{2}-15x+9=(x\\,-$\n{{field-1}}$)($\n{{field-2}}$x\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "We must factor the quadratic expression\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}-15x+9.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find two numbers that \n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant ($4\\times 9=36$), and\n\n- add to the linear coefficient ($-15$).\n\nSince the linear coefficient is negative and the product of the quadratic coefficient and constant is positive, we only need to consider the negative factor pairs of $36.$\n\nThe negative factor pairs of $36$ are\n\n$$\n(-1,-36),\\,(-2,-18),\\,(-3,-12),\\,(-4,-9),\\,(-6,-6).\n$$\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(-3,-12)$ add to $-15:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)+(-12) & =-15\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we write the linear term as $-3x-12x,$ and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-15x+9 & = \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-3x-12x+9 & = \\\\ (4{x}^{2}-3x)-(12x-9) & = \\\\ x(4x-3)-3(4x-3) & = \\\\ (x-3)(4x-3) & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f707b313-e9c4-51d8-ae46-03c5b10920ca" "answer-field-4f8e7b90-bd74-5dd6-b27c-58a4dbac0a72"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186061768 :answer-field/correct "answer-60d12287-da2e-5723-9891-def9ab5606f8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-60d12287-da2e-5723-9891-def9ab5606f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60d12287-da2e-5723-9891-def9ab5606f8" :answer/id #uuid "60d12287-da2e-5723-9891-def9ab5606f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f707b313-e9c4-51d8-ae46-03c5b10920ca" :answer-field/id #uuid "f707b313-e9c4-51d8-ae46-03c5b10920ca" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d3190ce8-8d61-5d10-b6da-2e9aeb1500b9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d3190ce8-8d61-5d10-b6da-2e9aeb1500b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3190ce8-8d61-5d10-b6da-2e9aeb1500b9" :answer/id #uuid "d3190ce8-8d61-5d10-b6da-2e9aeb1500b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4f8e7b90-bd74-5dd6-b27c-58a4dbac0a72" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f8e7b90-bd74-5dd6-b27c-58a4dbac0a72" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7dd80e3a-05e9-5e40-a54c-e5cfea2ecc75" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7dd80e3a-05e9-5e40-a54c-e5cfea2ecc75"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7dd80e3a-05e9-5e40-a54c-e5cfea2ecc75" :answer/id #uuid "7dd80e3a-05e9-5e40-a54c-e5cfea2ecc75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3b50cd1f-80a5-51f1-b3eb-2663a6e28812" :question/id #uuid "3b50cd1f-80a5-51f1-b3eb-2663a6e28812" :question/math-academy-id "q-224897" :question/problem "Factor the following quadratic expression.\n\n$20{b}^{2}-12b+1=(2b\\,-$\n{{field-1}}$)($\n{{field-2}}$b\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "We must factor the quadratic expression\n\n$$\n20{b}^{2}-12b+1.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find two numbers that \n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant ($20\\times 1=20$), and\n\n- add to the linear coefficient ($-12$).\n\nSince the linear coefficient is negative and the product of the quadratic coefficient and constant is positive, we only need to consider the negative factor pairs of $20.$\n\nThe negative factor pairs of $20$ are\n\n$$\n(-1,-20),\\,(-2,-10),\\,(-4,-5).\n$$\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(-2,-10)$ add to $-12:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)+(-10) & =-12\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we write the linear term as $-2b-10b,$ and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{b}^{2}-12b+1 & = \\\\ 20{b}^{2}-2b-10b+1 & = \\\\ (20{b}^{2}-2b)-(10b-1) & = \\\\ 2b(10b-1)-(10b-1) & = \\\\ (2b-1)(10b-1) & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4894e318-1ff2-5f50-b281-d62b33594a63" "answer-field-36a2e263-cd65-5517-af18-d6768ff0e51b" "answer-field-d93f8853-6923-594d-a9b4-a58c020bf26c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4894e318-1ff2-5f50-b281-d62b33594a63" :answer-field/id #uuid "4894e318-1ff2-5f50-b281-d62b33594a63" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5050617d-d60e-5d12-93de-50f83c35fc74" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5050617d-d60e-5d12-93de-50f83c35fc74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5050617d-d60e-5d12-93de-50f83c35fc74" :answer/id #uuid "5050617d-d60e-5d12-93de-50f83c35fc74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-36a2e263-cd65-5517-af18-d6768ff0e51b" :answer-field/id #uuid "36a2e263-cd65-5517-af18-d6768ff0e51b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1fb21ada-6744-5f70-b1dc-ecaec4ba734e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1fb21ada-6744-5f70-b1dc-ecaec4ba734e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1fb21ada-6744-5f70-b1dc-ecaec4ba734e" :answer/id #uuid "1fb21ada-6744-5f70-b1dc-ecaec4ba734e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d93f8853-6923-594d-a9b4-a58c020bf26c" :answer-field/id #uuid "d93f8853-6923-594d-a9b4-a58c020bf26c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b0647f1f-8929-5a4c-a972-69473a57b03a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b0647f1f-8929-5a4c-a972-69473a57b03a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0647f1f-8929-5a4c-a972-69473a57b03a" :answer/id #uuid "b0647f1f-8929-5a4c-a972-69473a57b03a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186065449 :tutorial/content "In a previous lesson, we learned how to factor quadratic trinomials whose quadratic coefficient equals one. In this lesson, we'll extend our understanding to include cases where the quadratic coefficient is a positive integer that's different from one.\n\nFor example, let's factor the following trinomial:\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{2}}x^2+{\\color{purple}{7}}x+{\\color{blue}{3}}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the quadratic coefficient equals ${\\color{red}{2}}.$\n\nTo factor this trinomial, we must find two numbers that \n\n- *multiply* to give the *product* of the quadratic coefficient and the constant $({\\color{red}{2}} \\times {\\color{blue}{3}} = 6),$ and\n\n- *add* to give the linear coefficient $({\\color{purple}{7}})$.\n\nWe can factor this trinomial in four steps:\n\n- **Step 1:**  We start by writing down the factor pairs of $6{:}$\n\nThe factor pairs of $6$ are\n\n$$\n(1,6), \\qquad (2,3).\n$$\n\n- **Step 2:**  Determine which of these factor pairs add up to the coefficient of the linear term $({\\color{purple}{7}})\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+6 & =7 & ✓ \\\\ 2+3 & =5 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 3:**  Using the factor pair identified in the previous step, write the linear term as $7x=x+6x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+7x+3 & = \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+x+6x+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 4:**  Factor the first two terms and the last two terms separately and then factor the expression completely:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+x+6x+3 & = \\\\ x(2x+1)+3(2x+1) & = \\\\ (2x+1)(x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd we're done! \n\nWe can check that our answer is correct by expanding the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2x+1)(x+3) & = \\\\ 2x\\cdot (x+3)+1\\cdot (x+3) & = \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+6x+x+3 & = \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+7x+3 & \\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186065450 :tutorial/content "To factor a quadratic expression, we must find a factor pair of the *product* of the quadratic coefficient and the constant that adds to the linear coefficient.\n\nWith that in mind, let's factor the following trinomial:\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{2}}y^2 {\\color{purple}{\\,-\\,7}}y + {\\color{blue}{3}}\n$$\n\nNotice that,\n\n- the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant, ${\\color{red}{2}} \\times {\\color{blue}{3}} = 6$, is *positive*, while\n\n- the coefficient of the linear term $({\\color{purple}{-7}})$ is *negative*.\n\nSince the linear coefficient is negative and the product of the quadratic coefficient and constant is positive, we need to consider the *negative* factor pairs of $6.$\n\nThe negative factor pairs of $6$ are\n\n$$\n(-1,-6), \\quad (-2,-3).\n$$\n\nFor each pair, their *product* is positive, and their sum is *negative*, which is what we want.\n\nNow, we determine which of these factor pairs sums to the coefficient of the linear term $({\\color{purple}{-7}}){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)+(-6) & =-7\\,✓ \\\\ (-2)+(-3) & =-5\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we write the linear term as $-y - 6y,$ and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-7y+3 & = \\\\ 2{y}^{2}-y-6y+3 & = \\\\ (2{y}^{2}-y)-(6y-3) & = \\\\ y(2y-1)-3(2y-1) & = \\\\ (y-3)(2y-1) & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064458 :activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "activity-573c8163-64a6-518f-9257-259186333e47" :activity/id #uuid "573c8163-64a6-518f-9257-259186333e47" :activity/title "Weighted Least-Squares" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049282 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-6e709a23-5648-505a-9cf2-c078b18494cd" "step-d99942ec-6a5c-5573-82e8-6cbe4cc7bec4" "step-751743ec-996c-5a2a-bfd6-fa0a4fc9b5c2" "step-702d868a-a1c8-52cb-817f-20990764bc4d" "step-410908c7-9a98-57f0-be29-8a517140c24f"] :activity/first-step "step-6e709a23-5648-505a-9cf2-c078b18494cd" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-6e709a23-5648-505a-9cf2-c078b18494cd" :step/id #uuid "6e709a23-5648-505a-9cf2-c078b18494cd" :step/content 17592186269153 :step/next "step-d99942ec-6a5c-5573-82e8-6cbe4cc7bec4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d99942ec-6a5c-5573-82e8-6cbe4cc7bec4" :step/id #uuid "d99942ec-6a5c-5573-82e8-6cbe4cc7bec4" :step/content 17592186388511 :step/next "step-751743ec-996c-5a2a-bfd6-fa0a4fc9b5c2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-751743ec-996c-5a2a-bfd6-fa0a4fc9b5c2" :step/id #uuid "751743ec-996c-5a2a-bfd6-fa0a4fc9b5c2" :step/content 17592186269158 :step/next "step-702d868a-a1c8-52cb-817f-20990764bc4d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-702d868a-a1c8-52cb-817f-20990764bc4d" :step/id #uuid "702d868a-a1c8-52cb-817f-20990764bc4d" :step/content 17592186278195 :step/next "step-410908c7-9a98-57f0-be29-8a517140c24f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-410908c7-9a98-57f0-be29-8a517140c24f" :step/id #uuid "410908c7-9a98-57f0-be29-8a517140c24f" :step/content 17592186381167 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166751 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a6139fff-4bc1-54e3-9731-cfafa322d577" "question-974d5dad-6c2d-5354-babc-ebd956728577"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166589 :question/problem "Consider the polynomials $p_1(t)$ and $p_2(t),$ given by\n\n$$\np_1(t)=3+2t, \\qquad\n\tp_2(t)=-t+t^2.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $\\mathcal{B}=\\big\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\big\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1, p_2 \\big\\},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}$ are ![](images/9e/9eca81c24ee88a63d1c5468160a118cb1e987793d5fdc8d2d7eaa317fadeda93.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1, p_2 \\big\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n![](images/8c/8c3fce8e9d7cc170ad66706e783c4a46ba0530c119b8b824a66d9b5850e62760.svg)\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =4\\cdot (3+2t)+(-3)\\cdot (-t+{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =12+8t+3t-3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =12+11t-3{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166752 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-04ab001d-eb12-502f-a292-54d2ac24e44a" "question-c4795a7a-dbd7-5cec-b948-e685d7225538"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166590 :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n![](images/b9/b9a1cb7eb2a3bcbadd73a68f9e73914e124a2359b8f8fc1ccc33ca950e714f88.svg)\nIf $\\mathcal B = \\{B_1,B_2\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{ B_1, B_2 \\},$ calculate ![](images/9b/9b978860f45e9e62e0315727c8eafac13360f29a7762480103b087ed6babf376.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\nx_1 B_1 +x_2 B_2 = A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} & -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n![](images/88/88ea80808ca87358b78cf322c8ddd81ad7f95ddc02526361aace1ca9b914d486.svg)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 18 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=18 \\\\ -{x}_{2}=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get $x_2 =9.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-9 & =-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, ![](images/c5/c57b6f1ce1762add9b5b5d3e15a6363f009482b12b12366434c090d6a7478c6b.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166753 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3f47118a-6b16-5a1a-918c-cf6f9d98f21a" "question-ed08ece1-de84-563e-9900-4e9012e55ca8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166591 :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\nx_1 p_1(t)+x_2 p_2(t) = q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(5+{t}^{2})+{x}_{2}(3t-2{t}^{2}) & =5-3t+3{t}^{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}t+({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}){t}^{2} & =5-3t+3{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n![](images/27/271f2b051a53f7aeae9a20ef23b97c9c903a7815f228dfa3ee23e2207bd24ee9.svg)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{5}){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first and second equations, we get $x_1=1$ and $x_2 =-1.$ Therefore, ![](images/1f/1fc60fff97ff92bd1cc515e6c984fbacb435dcf0fae24e751842eb8daf3390e8.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186360537 :question/problem "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=1-t+2{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t-{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =1\\cdot (1-t+2{t}^{2})+3\\cdot (t-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =1-t+2{t}^{2}+3t-3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =1+2t-{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186243938 :question/problem "$$\n{A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Find the matrix $C$ given that $B=\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of the matrix $C$ relative to $B$ are $[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in $\\text{Span}\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{A}_{1}+{x}_{2}{A}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-a6139fff-4bc1-54e3-9731-cfafa322d577" :question/id #uuid "a6139fff-4bc1-54e3-9731-cfafa322d577" :question/math-academy-id "q-106737" :question/problem "$$\n{A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Find the matrix $C$ given that $B=\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of the matrix $C$ relative to $B$ are $[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in $\\text{Span}\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{A}_{1}+{x}_{2}{A}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]+3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 4 \\\\ 8 & -12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3657d7a8-9e63-5bda-b364-5472d3ebc7e8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3657d7a8-9e63-5bda-b364-5472d3ebc7e8" :answer-field/id #uuid "3657d7a8-9e63-5bda-b364-5472d3ebc7e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-09368c8b-a900-5c28-b262-cad637c22752" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d30f044d-eab8-573d-9ea1-d54b5212aef6" "answer-09368c8b-a900-5c28-b262-cad637c22752" "answer-f0944f13-4475-5463-ad63-c07789ef499b" "answer-452b28d8-b289-5fff-a092-488eae620713" "answer-4d32b03a-dd94-5a69-92a8-4e06c57efc81"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d30f044d-eab8-573d-9ea1-d54b5212aef6" :answer/id #uuid "d30f044d-eab8-573d-9ea1-d54b5212aef6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09368c8b-a900-5c28-b262-cad637c22752" :answer/id #uuid "09368c8b-a900-5c28-b262-cad637c22752" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0944f13-4475-5463-ad63-c07789ef499b" :answer/id #uuid "f0944f13-4475-5463-ad63-c07789ef499b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 9 \\\\ 4 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-452b28d8-b289-5fff-a092-488eae620713" :answer/id #uuid "452b28d8-b289-5fff-a092-488eae620713" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d32b03a-dd94-5a69-92a8-4e06c57efc81" :answer/id #uuid "4d32b03a-dd94-5a69-92a8-4e06c57efc81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186243941 :question/problem "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=1+t+{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1+t-{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =(-1)\\cdot (1+t+{t}^{2})+1\\cdot (1+t-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =-1-t-{t}^{2}+1+t-{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-2{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-974d5dad-6c2d-5354-babc-ebd956728577" :question/id #uuid "974d5dad-6c2d-5354-babc-ebd956728577" :question/math-academy-id "q-95006" :question/problem "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=1+2t+3{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=-3-t-2{t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =3\\cdot (1+2t+3{t}^{2})+(-1)\\cdot (-3-t-2{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =3+6t+9{t}^{2}-(-3-t-2{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =6+7t+9{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-85e2bc47-da2a-5715-9eff-8bde08f41233"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-85e2bc47-da2a-5715-9eff-8bde08f41233" :answer-field/id #uuid "85e2bc47-da2a-5715-9eff-8bde08f41233" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-052ef4d9-7d83-566c-9540-57ab88c359e6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bfb4aaff-4675-5ecc-b60b-c88437151648" "answer-8a963e6d-9a8e-578a-a252-d9246861f62e" "answer-8bfc7edd-e7f0-56c8-b0a9-ec2e8d86072c" "answer-052ef4d9-7d83-566c-9540-57ab88c359e6" "answer-90b70d6e-2507-5294-8f1f-e52a10c64626"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfb4aaff-4675-5ecc-b60b-c88437151648" :answer/id #uuid "bfb4aaff-4675-5ecc-b60b-c88437151648" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p(t)=-6t+9{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a963e6d-9a8e-578a-a252-d9246861f62e" :answer/id #uuid "8a963e6d-9a8e-578a-a252-d9246861f62e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p(t)=5t+9{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8bfc7edd-e7f0-56c8-b0a9-ec2e8d86072c" :answer/id #uuid "8bfc7edd-e7f0-56c8-b0a9-ec2e8d86072c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p(t)=6+5t+9{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-052ef4d9-7d83-566c-9540-57ab88c359e6" :answer/id #uuid "052ef4d9-7d83-566c-9540-57ab88c359e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p(t)=6+7t+9{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90b70d6e-2507-5294-8f1f-e52a10c64626" :answer/id #uuid "90b70d6e-2507-5294-8f1f-e52a10c64626" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p(t)=7t+9{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186364716 :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -8 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -8 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & -4{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -8 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=-8 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -12 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 6{x}_{2}=-12 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2\\cdot (-2) & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1+4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+(-2)=1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-04ab001d-eb12-502f-a292-54d2ac24e44a" :question/id #uuid "04ab001d-eb12-502f-a292-54d2ac24e44a" :question/math-academy-id "q-106761" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}9 & -18 \\\\ 15 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -18 \\\\ 15 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & -2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -18 \\\\ 15 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-18 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -18 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 15\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -18 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 15\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{3}{2}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ -\\frac{{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=-3.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =9 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+(-3) & =9 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=6+(-3)=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ead372e1-7a0e-5867-a1cd-4c08293d91a3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ead372e1-7a0e-5867-a1cd-4c08293d91a3" :answer-field/id #uuid "ead372e1-7a0e-5867-a1cd-4c08293d91a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-82a88aba-0a9e-5b36-8e60-a1e8c2073da2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f6906166-88a4-5fdd-88ad-88c8265bc930" "answer-eda9481b-28f6-5a31-b610-2b56f853aa8e" "answer-1554fed7-affd-52c8-9b9d-11f75d6528f9" "answer-82a88aba-0a9e-5b36-8e60-a1e8c2073da2" "answer-b08ae541-af63-5e99-b15c-65086e6b98be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6906166-88a4-5fdd-88ad-88c8265bc930" :answer/id #uuid "f6906166-88a4-5fdd-88ad-88c8265bc930" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eda9481b-28f6-5a31-b610-2b56f853aa8e" :answer/id #uuid "eda9481b-28f6-5a31-b610-2b56f853aa8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1554fed7-affd-52c8-9b9d-11f75d6528f9" :answer/id #uuid "1554fed7-affd-52c8-9b9d-11f75d6528f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82a88aba-0a9e-5b36-8e60-a1e8c2073da2" :answer/id #uuid "82a88aba-0a9e-5b36-8e60-a1e8c2073da2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b08ae541-af63-5e99-b15c-65086e6b98be" :answer/id #uuid "b08ae541-af63-5e99-b15c-65086e6b98be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186243946 :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 20 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 20 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} & -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 20 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=20 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 20 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 20 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{3}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 7{x}_{2}=14 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2\\cdot 2 & =4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =8 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4+2=6.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-c4795a7a-dbd7-5cec-b948-e685d7225538" :question/id #uuid "c4795a7a-dbd7-5cec-b948-e685d7225538" :question/math-academy-id "q-106778" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then $2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} & 3{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ -{x}_{1}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}↔{R}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ {x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second,  third and fourth equations, we get ${x}_{2}=3.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3 & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, $2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2\\cdot 2+3=7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d571972e-d66f-51ff-ad55-ae539c035701"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d571972e-d66f-51ff-ad55-ae539c035701" :answer-field/id #uuid "d571972e-d66f-51ff-ad55-ae539c035701" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5a757e57-8827-5bbe-9ac1-63a3f529a76c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b0025512-e99f-5297-ba08-5bbf9b2b1291" "answer-48750a06-11eb-5111-88f7-360fb2f33835" "answer-87819992-b54e-5a67-ad9b-1e74d374d74c" "answer-5a757e57-8827-5bbe-9ac1-63a3f529a76c" "answer-128ce6e3-dc22-5943-ae78-9ca654be08a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0025512-e99f-5297-ba08-5bbf9b2b1291" :answer/id #uuid "b0025512-e99f-5297-ba08-5bbf9b2b1291" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48750a06-11eb-5111-88f7-360fb2f33835" :answer/id #uuid "48750a06-11eb-5111-88f7-360fb2f33835" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87819992-b54e-5a67-ad9b-1e74d374d74c" :answer/id #uuid "87819992-b54e-5a67-ad9b-1e74d374d74c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a757e57-8827-5bbe-9ac1-63a3f529a76c" :answer/id #uuid "5a757e57-8827-5bbe-9ac1-63a3f529a76c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-128ce6e3-dc22-5943-ae78-9ca654be08a8" :answer/id #uuid "128ce6e3-dc22-5943-ae78-9ca654be08a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186360538 :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2} & -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{3}{4}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{9}{2} & \\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ \\frac{9}{2}{x}_{2}=\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}{x}_{2}=-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=1.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+6\\cdot 1 & =-2 \\\\ 4{x}_{1} & =-8 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-2+1=-1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186360540 :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1-{t}^{2},\\,q(t)=2+3t+4{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2+t)+{x}_{2}(1-{t}^{2}) & =2+3t+4{t}^{2} \\\\ (2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+{x}_{1}t-{x}_{2}{t}^{2} & =2+3t+4{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}=3 \\\\ -{x}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-4.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}+(-4)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+(-4)=-1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186243963 :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)={t}^{2}+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}-2t+4,\\,{p}_{3}(t)={t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-2,\\,\\,q(t)=2+{t}^{2}+{t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}({t}^{2}+t)+{x}_{2}({t}^{2}-2t+4)+{x}_{3}({t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-2) & =2+{t}^{2}+{t}^{3} \\\\ (4{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})+({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})t+({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}){t}^{2}+{x}_{3}{t}^{3} & =2+{t}^{2}+{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{3}{4}){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n4{x}_{2}-2\\cdot 1=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2\\cdot 1=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and therefore ${x}_{1}=2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-3f47118a-6b16-5a1a-918c-cf6f9d98f21a" :question/id #uuid "3f47118a-6b16-5a1a-918c-cf6f9d98f21a" :question/math-academy-id "q-106783" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=1+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1-t+{t}^{2},\\,q(t)=4+2{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(1+t)+{x}_{2}(1-t+{t}^{2}) & =4+2{t}^{2} \\\\ ({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})t+{x}_{2}{t}^{2} & =4+2{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third  equations, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(2)=4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2+2=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-77937620-6a66-58b9-a30b-f689a9264f87"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-77937620-6a66-58b9-a30b-f689a9264f87" :answer-field/id #uuid "77937620-6a66-58b9-a30b-f689a9264f87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f46fff59-b92e-5209-93ce-3b657617aa18" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0c2c8aab-876d-5beb-969f-37e4397cc77b" "answer-b70925f5-b4ec-58fa-86b0-e31569e83883" "answer-7afabdb1-8cf6-5bb2-8ddb-f74a538d8214" "answer-f46fff59-b92e-5209-93ce-3b657617aa18" "answer-91c5c0e4-5b53-5efc-880e-e4be1aa2d6a5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c2c8aab-876d-5beb-969f-37e4397cc77b" :answer/id #uuid "0c2c8aab-876d-5beb-969f-37e4397cc77b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b70925f5-b4ec-58fa-86b0-e31569e83883" :answer/id #uuid "b70925f5-b4ec-58fa-86b0-e31569e83883" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7afabdb1-8cf6-5bb2-8ddb-f74a538d8214" :answer/id #uuid "7afabdb1-8cf6-5bb2-8ddb-f74a538d8214" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f46fff59-b92e-5209-93ce-3b657617aa18" :answer/id #uuid "f46fff59-b92e-5209-93ce-3b657617aa18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91c5c0e4-5b53-5efc-880e-e4be1aa2d6a5" :answer/id #uuid "91c5c0e4-5b53-5efc-880e-e4be1aa2d6a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186366601 :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=-6{t}^{3}+6t+12,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-3t-2,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=-3{t}^{2}+2t,\\,\\,q(t)=-9{t}^{3}+19t+18.\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(-6{t}^{3}+6t+12)+{x}_{2}({t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-3t-2)+{x}_{3}(-3{t}^{2}+2t) & =-9{t}^{3}+19t+18 \\\\ (-6{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}){t}^{3}+(-2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}){t}^{2}+(6{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})t+(12{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}) & =-9{t}^{3}+19t+18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-6{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 6{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=19 \\\\ 12{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 12 & -2 & 0 & 18\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 12 & -2 & 0 & 18\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-6{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-2{x}_{2}-3\\cdot 2=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n-6{x}_{1}+(-3)=-9\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ and therefore ${x}_{2}=-3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-ed08ece1-de84-563e-9900-4e9012e55ca8" :question/id #uuid "ed08ece1-de84-563e-9900-4e9012e55ca8" :question/math-academy-id "q-106859" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=1-t+{t}^{3},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1+t-{t}^{3},\\,{p}_{3}(t)=2+t+{t}^{2},\\,\\,q(t)=-2t-2{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(1-t+{t}^{3})+{x}_{2}(1+t-{t}^{3})+{x}_{3}(2+t+{t}^{2}) & =-2t-2{t}^{2} \\\\ ({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})+(-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})t+{x}_{3}{t}^{2}+({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}){t}^{3} & =-2t-2{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-1){R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the  third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n2{x}_{2}+3(-2)=-2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=2.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(2)+2(-2)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],$ and therefore ${x}_{1}=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-215b5472-cd3f-5ffe-a96f-7f68ed482331"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-215b5472-cd3f-5ffe-a96f-7f68ed482331" :answer-field/id #uuid "215b5472-cd3f-5ffe-a96f-7f68ed482331" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5efef7b1-861f-5e68-b8ca-5b2773c2e616" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a2f94199-aed6-56a4-b7d3-20591c70cc04" "answer-83012f55-7bea-5910-92fd-117843ef7a66" "answer-7703ce2f-e1d8-54db-a00d-63e3390949cb" "answer-5efef7b1-861f-5e68-b8ca-5b2773c2e616" "answer-adc246a5-558f-5836-8eea-ace518963371"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2f94199-aed6-56a4-b7d3-20591c70cc04" :answer/id #uuid "a2f94199-aed6-56a4-b7d3-20591c70cc04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83012f55-7bea-5910-92fd-117843ef7a66" :answer/id #uuid "83012f55-7bea-5910-92fd-117843ef7a66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7703ce2f-e1d8-54db-a00d-63e3390949cb" :answer/id #uuid "7703ce2f-e1d8-54db-a00d-63e3390949cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5efef7b1-861f-5e68-b8ca-5b2773c2e616" :answer/id #uuid "5efef7b1-861f-5e68-b8ca-5b2773c2e616" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-adc246a5-558f-5836-8eea-ace518963371" :answer/id #uuid "adc246a5-558f-5836-8eea-ace518963371" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186168064 :tutorial/content "We've already seen how to write the coordinates of a vector $\\mathbf v\\in \\mathbb R^n$ relative some general basis $\\mathcal B$ of $\\mathbb R^n.$ In this lesson, we will generalize this concept to abstract vector spaces.\n\nAs an example, consider the matrices $A_1$ and $A_2,$ given by\n\n![](images/28/2828c037a750f078b4d98b93248e800ec05d4899d7eb390dd135326314c44e70.svg)\n\nThe set $\\mathcal{B}=\\big\\{ A_1, A_2 \\big\\}$ is a basis of the vector space $V = \\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ A_1, A_2 \\big\\}.$ Now, suppose that the coordinates of the matrix $C$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}$ are \n\n![](images/2d/2db3ab1e4452eff2f19151cc87a805452433c7f305a80e5480c25241cba42c38.svg)\n\nLet's find the matrix $C$ using this information. \n\nAs usual, any vector in $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ A_1, A_2 \\big\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\nx_1 A_1  + x_2 A_2,\n$$\n\nwhere $x_1,x_2$ are the coordinates of the vector relative to the basis. \n\nIn our case, we have \n\n![](images/64/6489e130a9237881664e1649cc5408cdff87cfb12dcf44c0342b9961cdf7bc81.svg)\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]+4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 10\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & 12 \\\\ 8 & -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 10 \\\\ 8 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186168065 :tutorial/content "Suppose we fix a basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2, \\ldots, \\mathbf{b}_n \\}$ of a finite-dimensional vector space $V$ with scalars from $\\mathbb{R}$ (note that \"finite-dimensional\" means that the basis contains a finite number of elements). Then, we can represent any element $\\mathbf{v} \\in V$ using the coordinates of $\\mathbf{v}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B} \\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/c9/c9297a30f87baf08295a752cb23f2d314139508f875b4ffa2fffc8763656bd54.svg)\n\nThis defines a bijective mapping $\\phi: V\\to \\mathbb{R}^n.$ Moreover, this particular mapping has some nice properties:\n\n- $\\phi(\\mathbf{u}+\\mathbf{v}) = \\phi(\\mathbf{u}) + \\phi(\\mathbf{v})$ for any $\\mathbf{u}, \\mathbf{v} \\in V,$ and\n\n- $\\phi(\\alpha \\mathbf{v}) = \\alpha \\phi(\\mathbf{v})$ for any $\\mathbf{v} \\in V$ and any $\\alpha \\in \\mathbb{R}.$\n\nBecause of this, we say that $V$ is **isomorphic** to $\\mathbb{R}^n.$ Intuitively, this means that $V$ and $\\mathbb R^n$ have identical structures.\n\nSo, any finite-dimensional vector space is isomorphic to $\\mathbb{R}^n$ for some particular $n.$ This means that instead of studying all possible vector spaces, we can simply study only one family of vector spaces, namely $\\mathbb{R}^n$ for $n\\geq 1.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166996 :activity/expected-seconds 840.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167580 :step/math-academy-id 653397 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167581 :step/math-academy-id 653398 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167582 :step/math-academy-id 653401 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167583 :step/math-academy-id 653404 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167584 :step/math-academy-id 653407 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179800 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-35226f58-033d-50fc-9ed5-94472de795ca" "question-ab43471e-dafe-5dcf-b8bc-06037ed994ac"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-35226f58-033d-50fc-9ed5-94472de795ca" :question/id #uuid "35226f58-033d-50fc-9ed5-94472de795ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-128060" :question/problem "Find the value of $(-\\frac{3}{8})÷\\frac{1}{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "Dividing a negative number by a positive number gives a negative number. Hence, the result will be negative.\n\nTherefore, since \n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{8}÷\\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{3\\times 6}{8\\times 1}=\\frac{18}{8}=\\frac{9}{4},\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{3}{8})÷\\frac{1}{6}=-\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3589368a-bcb8-5009-b31d-b69be611aa69"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3589368a-bcb8-5009-b31d-b69be611aa69" :answer-field/id #uuid "3589368a-bcb8-5009-b31d-b69be611aa69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-15ba5d73-cfbf-5d35-89f4-a709f6e9f4ae" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2c669c68-aefe-5e7c-b2c5-c63d2b25d4ca" "answer-76a67f28-627f-53d2-bf6b-8d0da5300ff8" "answer-15ba5d73-cfbf-5d35-89f4-a709f6e9f4ae" "answer-700bdd4a-0eec-5a10-a0a6-451aa0f53abd" "answer-3c34cd61-57c9-53a6-a30c-553a2947ad18"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c669c68-aefe-5e7c-b2c5-c63d2b25d4ca" :answer/id #uuid "2c669c68-aefe-5e7c-b2c5-c63d2b25d4ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76a67f28-627f-53d2-bf6b-8d0da5300ff8" :answer/id #uuid "76a67f28-627f-53d2-bf6b-8d0da5300ff8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15ba5d73-cfbf-5d35-89f4-a709f6e9f4ae" :answer/id #uuid "15ba5d73-cfbf-5d35-89f4-a709f6e9f4ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-700bdd4a-0eec-5a10-a0a6-451aa0f53abd" :answer/id #uuid "700bdd4a-0eec-5a10-a0a6-451aa0f53abd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c34cd61-57c9-53a6-a30c-553a2947ad18" :answer/id #uuid "3c34cd61-57c9-53a6-a30c-553a2947ad18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ab43471e-dafe-5dcf-b8bc-06037ed994ac" :question/id #uuid "ab43471e-dafe-5dcf-b8bc-06037ed994ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-128062" :question/problem "Determine the value of $(-\\frac{1}{5})÷(-\\frac{3}{10}).$" :question/worked-solution "Dividing a negative number by a negative number gives a positive number. Hence, the result will be positive.\n\nTherefore, since \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}÷\\frac{3}{10}=\\frac{1\\times 10}{5\\times 3}=\\frac{10}{15}=\\frac{2}{3},\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{1}{5})÷(-\\frac{3}{10})=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7774d184-d47b-5051-8e81-b32b977ef33a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7774d184-d47b-5051-8e81-b32b977ef33a" :answer-field/id #uuid "7774d184-d47b-5051-8e81-b32b977ef33a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6f8353d3-9579-5c1e-8802-4ea1bdff86fd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ce613343-8043-5bc1-ae12-aad3ccc46878" "answer-424b2dd8-9b73-548c-